# Source: en.wiktionary.org, https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blwyddyn.
# blwyddyn (feminine), plural blynyddoedd, with the DEDICATED count
# form blynedd used directly after a numeral.  That count form is the
# richest mutation case in the language's temporal vocabulary: it
# surfaces three ways depending on which numeral precedes it --
#   blynedd   radical, after three ("tair blynedd")
#   flynedd   soft b -> f, after two ("dwy flynedd")
#   mlynedd   nasal b -> m, after five ("pum mlynedd")
# all three attested: the first in running text on cy.wikipedia.org,
# the latter two on the en.wiktionary.org entry itself.
# Soft-mutated surfaces are listed beside the radical: Welsh changes a
# word's first letter after a preceding trigger.  Mutation table:
# en.wikipedia.org, "Welsh mutation".
# A Welsh numeral is followed by the singular (or, for the year, its count
# form), so both the counted forms and the ordinary plural are surfaces of
# this unit.
blwyddyn
flwyddyn
blynedd
flynedd
mlynedd
blynyddoedd
blynyddau
